      "value": {
        "evidence": "The seatback, torso restraint and seated thighs are visible, and one rear machine foot touches the salt bed. The specified human boot-to-cockpit-floor contacts are hidden. The closest machine limb is cropped before its ground endpoint, so the complete reviewed support footprint is not observable. This is a visibility failure, not a diagnosis of impossible hidden support.",
