    },
    {
      "value": {
        "evidence": "Local contacts are coherent: a forearm rests on the sill and the opposite hand lies on the map over a thigh. Owner-relative sides are reversed from the exact final prompt: the sill arm is the pilot anatomical RIGHT (image left), while the map hand is anatomical LEFT (image right). The prompt specified left forearm on sill and right hand on map; intended contact assignment therefore fails.",
